   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty good, thanks for asking.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.44,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm learning Spanish. Would watching films actually help?",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes, especially if you're past the absolute beginner stage. You'll hear real speed, accents and slang.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 0.69,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm about a year in.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.98,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Great level for it. Start with Spanish audio and Spanish subtitles, so you can see the words as you hear them.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.52,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Not English subtitles?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.34,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "English subtitles are fine for fun, but your brain will just read them. Spanish ones keep you learning.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 1.11,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Wait a second, any kind of film work best? I",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 1.03,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "tried a drama and got totally lost.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 1.91,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "kind": "wait_like",
   "phrasing": "waitlike_16",
   "block": "movies.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Comedies and family films are easier, the language is simpler and the action tells you what's going on. Rewatching a film you already know in English is a great trick too.",
   "est_sec": 9.71,
